WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
Being a manager used to mean one thing. Now it means everything.

2
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:11.990
Flatter orgs, bigger teams. And on top of that, you still have to deliver, like everyone else.

3
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:18.980
You're expected to know each person. What they're on. Where they want to go. What you promised two weeks ago.

4
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.280
All of it lives in your head. Until it doesn't.

5
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.980
So you walk into 1:1s unprepared.

6
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.420
Your team notices. You feel underwater.

7
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:35.020
And review season starts from a blank page.

8
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.350
That's why we built

9
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:37.970
Tainure.

10
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.470
Paste your notes after a meeting.

11
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.600
Tainure turns them into memory.

12
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.370
What was said, what you owe, what to raise next.

13
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.930
Before each 1:1, your prep is ready.

14
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.500
One person to the next, without the mental load.

15
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.010
It knows where each person wants to go, and what to coach next.

16
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:03.340
Have a question? Just ask. Tainure answers from everything you've captured.

17
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.590
It shows you who's slipping, before they slip.

18
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.890
And when review season comes, the evidence is already there.

19
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.090
Private to you. Nobody else reads it.

20
00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.910
A team that feels seen.

21
00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.450
A manager above water again.

22
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.530
Both of them growing.

23
00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:23.020
Tainure.

24
00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.440
Remember everything about the people you manage.
